<item>
            <title>[LU-20949] Encrypted buffered write fails with -EINVAL when another thread unlocks the folio during encryption</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20949</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;With client encryption, a buffered write to an encrypted file can fail on the client due to a failed lock check in &lt;tt&gt;osc_encrypt_pagecache_blocks()&lt;/tt&gt;. &lt;tt&gt;osc_brw_prep_request()&lt;/tt&gt; then returns -EINVAL, and the whole write RPC fails. A file small enough to be written by a single RPC ends up empty (0 bytes), and rewriting it usually succeeds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;osc_brw_prep_request()&lt;/tt&gt; checks for a lock on the folio (and takes it if not already locked). But other threads can take the folio lock for a short time while the folio is under writeback, and release it before the check in &lt;tt&gt;osc_encrypt_pagecache_blocks()&lt;/tt&gt;, e.g. a page fault through mmap, memory management related tasks such as reclaim, migration and compaction in async mode, invalidate_mapping_pages()/mapping_evict_folio() (e.g. drop_caches), and the readahead/filemap_read helpers.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
